ite error test\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full stitch task prompt with all project context, SRDs, architecture, execution constitution, task description, constraints, and acceptance criteria for implementing srd064-shuf R4.1-R4.4.\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools. [...] Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement R4.1-R4.4 for cmd/shuf (the main task)\n   - Modify `cmd/shuf/main.go` if any exit code handling changes are needed\n   - Add differential test cases to `cmd/shuf/shuf_test.go` covering R4.1-R4.4\n   - Run `go build -o bin/shuf ./cmd/shuf/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/shuf/...` to verify no issues (AC2)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/shuf/... -count=1` to verify tests pass (AC3)\n   - Verify all four requirements R4.1-R4.4 are implemented (AC4)\n   - Verify existing tests continue to pass (AC5)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, shuf_test.go) and was about to plan and implement the changes. The implementation was not yet started - no code was written or modified.\n\n   The existing code already handles R4.1 (exit 0 on success) and R4.2 (exit 1 on errors). The main work is adding differential tests that explicitly verify exit codes and ensuring comprehensive coverage per R4.3 and R4.4. Key additions needed:\n   - Differential tests with `ExitCode: 1` for error cases (invalid range, -i with files, -e with -i)\n   - Possibly additional differential tests to fill any gaps in the R4.4 coverage list\n   - Possibly a write error scenario test\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Implement the R4.1-R4.4 requirements by modifying `cmd/shuf/main.go` (if needed) and `cmd/shuf/shuf_test.go` (adding new differential tests for error exit codes and comprehensive coverage). Then verify with `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test`.\n\n   The task description states: \"Implement srd064-