{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PVsYwjupsZ4AsQnqrhdgTG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `compareOutputs` function compares stdout, stderr, and exit code between the Go binary and the reference binary. The `Normalize` functions are applied to both stdout and stderr before comparison.\n\nFor error cases, the stderr messages will differ between `shuf:` (our binary) and `gshuf:` (GNU binary), plus potentially different wording. So for differential tests on error cases, I need a normalizer that strips the binary name prefix from stderr messages.\n\nLet me now figure out what's missing and what to add.\n\n**Gap analysis for R4.1-R4.4:**\n\nR4.1 (exit 0 on success): Already implemented in main.go. \n\nThe existing differential tests all use `ExitCode: 0` which verifies this against gshuf, so that's covered. ✓\n\nR4.2 (exit 1 on error): Already implemented in main.go, but I need to add differential tests that verify error cases return exit code 1 matching gshuf's behavior.\n\nR4.3 (structural property verification): Already done with sortLines and lineCount normalizers. ✓\n\nR4.4 (comprehensive test coverage): Looking at what's covered—shuffle stdin lines, shuffle file lines, and the -i flag tests—I need to verify all the key scenarios are represented.\n\nI'm missing differential tests for -r repeat mode and error cases like invalid ranges or -i with files. For error cases, the stderr messages will differ between `shuf:` and `gshuf:` prefixes, so I'll need a normalizer that strips the program name to compare just the error content itself.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1845,"cache_read_input_tokens":44243,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1845},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"contex