ttempting to open any files.\n\nFor differential testing, I need both binaries to run in the same temp directory so that a nonexistent file like `somefile` produces the same \"extra operand\" error in both, rather than different file-not-found errors.\n\nI'm also considering how `discardStderr` works in these tests—comparing only stdout and exit codes gives us a structural property check that should hold across both implementations.\n\nWriting differential test for repeat mode... Writing test assertions... I need to check if \"errors\" is already in the imports, and if not, add it. Then I'll implement the three key additions: differential tests for error exit codes, a differential test for repeat mode completeness, and explicit exit code 1 verification in the standalone error tests. Adding exit code checks to remaining tests...\n\nFor write errors, the SIGPIPE handler already covers the main case, so I'll skip explicit write error testing since it's hard to test portably and would be fragile. Now I'll implement all these edits.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5826,"cache_read_input_tokens":52645,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5826},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78073c1a-ebc5-4b9f-bc7d-14f2b828e657","uuid":"0850d194-ebfd-462c-9e59-4b23b8dad404"}
